From 2bc8fd35f61b82ec6f281ab87d8fe84300fbfcbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:49:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] waylandhost: add a compositor for client surfaces

Kodi owns the display, the GPU context and the input devices, so a
browser or any other application has no way to show its output inside
Kodi's screen. Add a small Wayland compositor without a screen of its
own: clients connect through socket pairs handed to the processes the
host spawns, their dmabuf buffers are passed to an observer which draws
them, and keyboard and pointer events are injected by Kodi.

The host implements wl_compositor, wl_shm, wl_output, wl_seat,
xdg_wm_base for fullscreen toplevels, linux-dmabuf v4 with the format
table and device feedback Mesa needs to pick the render node,
wp_presentation and text-input v3. It runs its event loop on its own
thread; everything crossing into it is posted as a task. Child
processes are watched through pidfds; stopping the host terminates
them, closes their display connections, which ends a client that
ignores the signal at its next dispatch, and waits for each child's
exit. Buffers are released to the client once the surface no longer
shows them and every consumer has let go of them. The keyboard focus
goes to the surface mapped last, the pointer follows it, and a surface
losing the focus gets the leave events.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
